# Part 4 — Essential Docker Concepts

| Concept        | Description                                                   |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Image          | A template used to create containers                          |
| Container      | An isolated runtime instance created from an image            |
| Volume         | Persistent storage managed by Docker                          |
| Bind mount     | A mapping between a host path and a container path            |
| Network        | A mechanism for connecting containers                         |
| Dockerfile     | Instructions for building an image                            |
| Docker Compose | A tool for defining and managing multi-container applications |
| Port mapping   | Forwarding traffic from a host port to a container port       |
| Docker Engine  | The service responsible for managing Docker resources         |

