# Part 5 — Security Best Practices

* Avoid running containers in privileged mode unless required.
* Avoid exposing the Docker daemon to untrusted networks.
* Never mount the Docker socket into untrusted containers.
* Prefer trusted, maintained images.
* Avoid hardcoding passwords and API tokens in images or source-controlled files.
* Use resource limits where appropriate.
* Apply the principle of least privilege.
* Review published ports and mounted host directories.
* Remember that containers share the host kernel and are not equivalent to full virtual machines.

